  "final_answer": "I have all the information needed. Let me provide the final answer.\n\n## Answer\n\nBased on Wolfram|Alpha calculations (using the Consumer Price Index), $10,000 US dollars today is worth:\n\n| Year | Equivalent Value of Today's $10,000 |\n|------|-------------------------------------|\n| **1980** | **$2,514.25** (1980 USD) |\n| **1970** | **$1,184.54** (1970 USD) |\n\n### Additional Details:\n- **1980**: Average inflation rate of 3.05% per year; total inflation factor of 297.7%\n- **1970**: Average inflation rate of 3.88% per year; total inflation factor of 744.2%\n\n### Summary:\n- In **1980**, $10,000 of today's money would have been equivalent to approximately **$2,514.25** in 1980 dollars.\n- In **1970**, $10,000 of today's money would have been equivalent to approximately **$1,184.54** in 1970 dollars.\n\nThis shows that the purchasing power of the US dollar has decreased substantially over time — $1 in 1980 had nearly 4 times the buying power of today's dollar, and $1 in 1970 had over 8 times the buying power of today's dollar.",
